  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member writing a reply, I want a smiley picked in the smiley picker to be inserted where my cursor is, so that I can put it in the middle of my text. Operator feedback (device, 2026-11-15): whatever the cursor position, the smiley is added at the **end** of the message, which is wrong.\n\n### Expected\n- The smiley code is inserted at the caret. If text is selected, it replaces the selection.\n- The caret is placed right after the inserted smiley, and focus comes back to the editor.\n- The same caret rule holds for every insertion from a sheet that takes focus (smiley, GIF, image): insert at the caret, or replace a selection.\n- **Formatting tags are different: they never replace a selection, they wrap it.** `[b]` + selection + `[/b]`. With no selection they are inserted at the caret, and the caret lands between the opening and the closing tag. A fix here must not turn wrapping into replacing.\n\n### Where to look (read from `dev-swift`; the cause is not established)\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Composer/ReplyComposerView.swift`:\n  - `openSmileys()` (~:179) captures the caret in `rangeForSmiley = selectedRange` before presenting the sheet;\n  - `insertSmiley(_:)` (:188) calls `model.insert(smiley:replacing: rangeForSmiley)`.\n- Likely suspects:\n  - the editor lost focus before `selectedRange` was read, so the captured range is nil or at the end;\n  - the `TextEditor(selection:)` binding was not up to date;\n  - `model.insert(smiley:replacing:)` falls back to the end when the range is nil.\n- `ReplyTextInsertionEngine.insert(_:into:selectedUTF16Range:)` (:206) inserts at a range: check that the smiley path really reaches it with the captured range.\n- Check both composers: the default one and the experimental « Composer moderne » (#903/#904), as #909 does for the picker's first tap.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] With the caret in the middle of a line, a picked smiley lands at the caret; with a selection, it replaces it; the caret ends right after it.\n- [ ] A formatting tag applied to a selection still wraps it (text kept), at its real position, not at the end.\n- [ ] Same for a smiley picked after scrolling the editor, and with the keyboard hidden before opening the picker.\n- [ ] A test pins the rule. A model or engine test is red today if the captured range is lost, and a hosted test goes through the real open → pick path if feasible.\n\nRelated: #909 (picker closes on first tap), #600 (picker sections), LOT-104 (#195).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n\n",
